WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.975
Last, the sea that comes from behind.

2
00:00:03.225 --> 00:00:07.350
Following seas are especially dangerous for small powerboats.

3
00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:13.025
A broach happens when a wave from astern lifts your stern and slews the boat sideways.

4
00:00:13.275 --> 00:00:16.475
Now you’re beam-on, and the next wave can roll you.

5
00:00:16.725 --> 00:00:21.150
In the worst case, the bow digs in and the stern goes over the top.

6
00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:23.175
That’s a pitchpole.

7
00:00:23.425 --> 00:00:28.250
So when you run before big seas, or come in an inlet, where do you put the boat?

8
00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:31.050
On the back of a wave.

9
00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:33.500
Match its speed and stay there.

10
00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:35.725
Don’t surf down the face.

11
00:00:35.975 --> 00:00:40.600
Raise the trim tabs to keep the bow up, and keep a hand on the throttle.

12
00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:42.750
That’s lesson six.

13
00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:44.625
Know your hull.

14
00:00:44.875 --> 00:00:48.850
Clear scuppers, double clamps, a plug at every through-hull.

15
00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:52.050
Find it, stop it, pump it, call early.

16
00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:54.375
And ride the back of the wave.

17
00:00:54.625 --> 00:00:58.050
Next time: making the boat go where you want her to.
